            <ArticleTitle>[Efficacy of a single dose of praziquantel as treatment for Taenia saginata and Hymenolepis nana].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>759-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cestodes are very frequent intestinal parasites. They induce different troubles, regrouped as &quot;taeniasis&quot;. In our study, 30 patients with Taenia saginata and 10 with Hymenolepis nana has been treated by one single dose of praziquantel, a wide-spectrum anti-helminthic drug, at the dosage of 10 mg/kg/day and 20 mg/kg/day respectively. As side-effects, no biological disturbances occurred, but 6 patients complained of abdominal pain and diarrhea. The efficiency has been complete. Praziquantel seems to be the drug of choice as treatment of adult cestodes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
